<h1>Macro Syntax</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Macro commands in KUBE obey the following rules:</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>1. KUBE macros are not case sensitive. For example,</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>SelAll</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>selall</b></span>, and <span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>SELALL</b></span> refers to the same command.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>2. Blank spaces are ignored (with the exception when they appear in values within quotes). For example, the following macros are equivalent:</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoise( Strength = 10 )</b></span> &#160;and &#160;<span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoiseAvg(Strength=10)</b></span>.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>3. If a macro does not contain parameters it can be typed with or without brackets. For example,</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>SelAll</b></span> or <span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>SelAll()</b></span>.</p>
<p>If a macro contains parameters then it can be typed in three ways. For example:</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoiseAvg</b></span> – the corresponding dialog will appear.</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoiseAvg()</b></span> – the macro will be executed with the default parameter(s).</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoiseAvg( Strength=10 )</b></span> – the macro will be executed with the designated parameter(s).</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>4. Parameter name may be omitted. For example,</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoiseAvg( 10 )</b></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>MshRedNoiseAvg( Strength=10 )</b></span> are equivalent.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>5. If a parameter is missing, its default value is used. For example, <span style="margin-left:40px; font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>RedNoiseByCrv( Strength=M, Angle=N )</b></span> <span style="margin-left:40px;">can be invoked in the following ways:</span></p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>RedNoiseByCrv()</b></span> – the macro will be executed with the default values of Strength and Angle parameters.</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>RedNoiseByCrv( 3 )</b></span> – the macro will be executed with Strength=3 and the default value for Angle.</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>RedNoiseByCrv( 4, 12 )</b></span> – the macro will be executed with Strength=4 and Angle=12.</p>
<p class="whs4"><span style="font-weight:bold; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><b>RedNoiseByCrv( Angle=5 )</b></span> – the macro will be executed with the default value for Strength and Angle=5.</p>
<p class="whs5">&#160;</p>
<p class="whs5">Syntax of KUBE macros can be represented by the following diagram:</p>
